{
  "id": "adjective-endings-1",
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "Adjektivendungen 1",
  "group": "Adjectives",
  "sourceFile": "adjektivendungen1.html",
  "overviewSource": "adjektivendungenexpl.html",
  "overview": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "An adjective before a noun needs an ending. After a der-word, the article already shows gender/case, so the adjective usually takes weak -e or -en."
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "",
        "rows": [
          [
            "After der-word",
            "Masc.",
            "Fem.",
            "Neut.",
            "Plural"
          ],
          [
            "Nominative",
            "-e",
            "-e",
            "-e",
            "-en"
          ],
          [
            "Accusative",
            "-en",
            "-e",
            "-e",
            "-en"
          ],
          [
            "Dative",
            "-en",
            "-en",
            "-en",
            "-en"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "The five common -e cells are nominative singular and accusative feminine/neuter. Almost everything else after a der-word is -en."
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "content": "",
        "de": "Der neue Computer ist teuer. Ich kaufe den neuen Computer nicht.",
        "note": "nom. masc. -e · acc. masc. -en"
      }
    ]
  },
